---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro";

const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", href: "/" },
  { name: "Colophon", href: "/colophon" },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Colophon: How This Site Is Built"
  description="How urielpapa.com is built: Astro static pages, Tailwind CSS, the Keystatic git-based CMS, Vercel hosting, JSON-LD, Markdown copies and llms.txt for AI tools."
>
  <div class="app-layout max-w-read pt-8">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
    <h1 class="h1">Colophon</h1>
    <div class="app-prose mt-6">
      <p>
        This page explains how urielpapa.com is put together. It doubles as a
        small, working example of the SEO, GEO and AEO ideas I write about.
      </p>
      <h2 id="stack">What is it built with?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Framework:</strong>
          <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>, started from the open-source <a
            href="https://github.com/satnaing/astro-paper">AstroPaper</a
          > theme by Sat Naing and reworked into a black and white design.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Styling:</strong> Tailwind CSS 4, with light and dark themes that
          follow your system setting.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Content and CMS:</strong> posts are Markdown and MDX files in the
          Git repository, edited through <a href="https://keystatic.com"
            >Keystatic</a
          >.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Hosting:</strong> static pages on Vercel's CDN. Only the contact
          form and newsletter signup run on the server.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Search:</strong>
          <a href="https://pagefind.app">Pagefind</a>, a static search index
          built at deploy time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Fonts:</strong> Bricolage Grotesque for headings, Albert Sans for
          text and JetBrains Mono for code, all self-hosted.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="speed">Why is it so light?</h2>
      <p>
        Pages are plain HTML and CSS. The only JavaScript is small and optional:
        the theme switch, search, copying code, sharing, and progressive
        enhancement for the forms. Everything still works without it.
      </p>
      <h2 id="machines">
        How is it made readable for search engines and AI tools?
      </h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Structured data (JSON-LD) on every page: WebSite and Person
          everywhere, BlogPosting on posts, breadcrumbs, and FAQ only where the
          questions are visible.
        </li>
        <li>
          A plain Markdown copy of every post at the same address plus <code
            >.md</code
          >, marked noindex so it never competes with the page.
        </li>
        <li>
          A generated <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a> summary, a full <a
            href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a
          > and an XML <a href="/sitemap-index.xml">sitemap</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          A <a href="/robots.txt">robots.txt</a> that welcomes search, AI search and
          AI training crawlers.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="privacy">What does it track?</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing by default. If analytics is switched on, it loads only after you
        interact with the page and records page views plus a few events such as
        newsletter signups.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
